1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,000
[roars]

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Strange beasts

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,000
and monsters.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Vast riches.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Hidden treasures.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Evil haunts.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Uncharted frontiers.

8
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
The mysterious unknown.

9
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,000
The people who are captivated by the magic
in those words...

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
are called...

11
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Hunters.

12
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:36,000
[theme song playing]

13
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,000
[gasps]

14
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Sorry, I was careless
and he got away.

15
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:11,000
[Hisoka] Don't lie to me.

16
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:14,000
He probably begged you to grant him
a last request

17
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:18,000
and you relented.
Am I right?

18
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,000
[Gitarrackur]
Well, I may have felt sorry for the man.

19
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,000
He was going to die anyway.

20
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:27,000
You really need to stop pitying those
who serve no purpose.

21
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:30,000
I do have standards.

22
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Why waste time on people
who are utterly useless.

23
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:37,000
I only spare those
whose premature deaths would be a waste.

24
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:43,000
DEFEAT x AND x DISGRACE

25
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,000
[narrator]
Hisoka targets Kurapika and Leorio

26
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,000
as Gon goes after Hisoka's badge.

27
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,000
Under the dark silent cover of night,

28
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:55,000
something is about to happen.

29
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,000
[crickets chirping]

30
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Now, run!

31
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:33,000
[cries out]

32
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:39,000
Yes, I remember them.

33
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,000
This should be fun.

34
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:01,000
[Gon]
It looks like Hisoka's found his prey.

35
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:09,000
[grunts]
Leorio, Kurapika.

36
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:16,000
I never thought he'd be going after
Leorio and Kurapika.

37
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:18,000
What am I supposed to do now?

38
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:21,000
Don't lose focus. Stick to the plan!

39
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:24,000
And the moment Hisoka attacks,
go for his badge.

40
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:27,000
That's the best chance
I'm going to get to take it.

41
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:28,000
It's my only chance.

42
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:37,000
[panting]

43
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,000
No, I can't.

44
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:44,000
if they start fighting,
I'll have to change my strategy.

45
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:52,000
[Leorio] All right, so,
I finally figured out who my target is.

46
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:57,000
But how am I supposed to find her
on an island this big?

47
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:01,000
Isn't wandering around like this
a huge waste of energy?

48
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:05,000
No more a waste of energy
than constantly whining, I would imagine.

49
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:08,000
Well you've already got your six points
so you're all set.

50
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:11,000
But I'm plumb out of luck
if I don't find my target pretty soon.

51
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,000
[both grunt]

52
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Hey.

53
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:19,000
Hisoka.

54
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,000
What a coincidence meeting you here.

55
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:23,000
How fortunate.

56
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:27,000
[laughs] Why do I run into people
I don't want to see?

57
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:31,000
You see, all I'm lacking
is just two more points.

58
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:34,000
I was hoping you might give me yours.

59
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,000
Give you what?

60
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,000
You're crazy. I'm not going to give--

61
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,000
Leorio.

62
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:41,000
You said you only need two points.

63
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:45,000
Meaning neither one of us
is your primary target.

64
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:46,000
Am I right about that?

65
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:49,000
Leave the questions to me, all right?

66
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:52,000
Will you give me your badges?
Answer carefully.

67
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,000
I suppose that depends...

68
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:01,000
Between the two of us
we currently have four badges.

69
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:05,000
Mine, my target's, Leorio's,

70
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:08,000
and one that's worth only a single point
to either him or me.

71
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:13,000
Of the four, two might possibly belong
to your specific target,

72
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:14,000
and only two.

73
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:18,000
Mine or the badge
that's worth a single point.

74
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:22,000
Leorio's number is 403.

75
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:25,000
He was targeted by number 16,
Tonpa.

76
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:26,000
And he,

77
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:30,000
number 16, was assigned to me
as my target.

78
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:33,000
Each of us was given a different target

79
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,000
so 16 and 403 are out.

80
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,000
[Hisoka] Indeed.

81
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:42,000
Neither of those is the target
I was searching for.

82
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:43,000
What of it?

83
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,000
[Kurapika]
That just leaves the other two badges.

84
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:50,000
If you're willing to take the badge
that's worth one point and leave

85
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:52,000
you are more than welcome to have it.

86
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:56,000
But I will not allow you to take mine.

87
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:00,000
And the same goes for the other two.

88
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:05,000
If you insist on taking them by force

89
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:09,000
prepare to fight me for them.

90
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,000
[chuckles]

91
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:38,000
-[Hisoka laughs]
-[Kurapika and Leorio gasp]

92
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,000
[purrs]

93
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:55,000
Out of curiosity, what is your number?

94
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,000
Four hundred and four.

95
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:06,000
[Hisoka] Very well.

96
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:10,000
You have yourself a deal.

97
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:12,000
I'll take the badge worth a single point.

98
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:14,000
[gasps]

99
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,000
I'll leave it here.

100
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,000
Don't look so concerned.

101
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:28,000
I'll stay right here
until you're out of sight.

102
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:44,000
[laughs]

103
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:49,000
In a few short days,
they've both grown beyond recognition.

104
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:51,000
But, they have more to learn.

105
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:55,000
I wonder...
why must unripe fruit be so...

106
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:57,000
tantalizing.

107
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:00,000
Such a pity.

108
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,000
Not the badge I was hoping for.

109
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:06,000
[exhales with relief]

110
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,000
[Gon]
That was a close one.

111
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:15,000
But now,
I've only got one more chance left.

112
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:19,000
Whenever he finds his next prey,
I'll be ready.

113
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:31,000
Hey.

114
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,000
Wait just a minute.

115
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:37,000
What if the next person he finds decides
that they don't want to fight him either?

116
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:46,000
Oh man.

117
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:50,000
If the next person just surrenders
and hands over their badge,

118
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:53,000
like what I just saw happen,
I won't get another chance at all.

119
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,000
I'm so stupid!

120
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:09,000
Geez, why didn't I think of that?
[groans]

121
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:11,000
[Hisoka sighs]

122
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:12,000
[gasps]

123
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,000
[birds cawing]

124
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:20,000
[wind blowing]

125
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,000
[squeaking]

126
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:34,000
[whimpers]
I'm so scared.

127
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:36,000
I don't want to be here anymore.

128
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,000
I feel his bloodlust.

129
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:45,000
[groans] Oh no...

130
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:50,000
They had to go
and get me stirred up,

131
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:53,000
there's only one thing to do about it now.

132
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:57,000
I have to quell it.

133
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:59,000
[moans]

134
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,000
[birds chirping]

135
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:32,000
[waves crashing gently]

136
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:46,000
[whimpers softly]

137
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:50,000
[Hisoka] Well.

138
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,000
Time to go.

139
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:56,000
I can do this.

140
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:00,000
His bloodlust is gone.

141
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:03,000
but that look in his eyes
is nothing like before.

142
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,000
He's going to attack the next person
he sees,

143
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:09,000
even if they try to surrender,
I'm sure of it.

144
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:14,000
I know, I've got to move ahead
and find his next prey before he does.

145
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:20,000
Then, I need to find myself
a good spot to hide

146
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:22,000
and wait for my chance.

147
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,000
There!

148
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:46,000
I've only got about a minute or so
before Hisoka spots it.

149
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:50,000
I need to figure out where
their paths are going to cross.

150
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:54,000
Got it!

151
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:58,000
Gotta hurry.

152
00:12:59,000 --> 00:12:59,000
[grunts]

153
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:05,000
Hisoka will attack
the second he notices that guy.

154
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:08,000
If I want to steal his badge,
this is it.

155
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:11,000
It's the last chance I'm going to get.

156
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:29,000
HUNTER GLOSSARY

157
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:33,000
CHANCE

158
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:36,000
[waves crashing gently]

159
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:55,000
[footsteps]

160
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:05,000
[Gon] It feels like Hisoka has
completely hidden his presence.

161
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:15,000
He's going to find me.
I just know it!

162
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:17,000
[panting]

163
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:25,000
I'll have to conceal my presence too.

164
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:30,000
[footsteps]

165
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:39,000
[footsteps audible]

166
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:41,000
[complete silence]

167
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:46,000
[footsteps audible]

168
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:48,000
[complete silence]

169
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:53,000
[Gon] I have to stay hidden.
I can't let him sense me.

170
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:57,000
Focus.

171
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:06,000
Hmm?

172
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:10,000
[rumbling]

173
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:11,000
Here he comes.

174
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:13,000
[grunts]

175
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:16,000
[man] Hisoka!

176
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:19,000
Damn it. Bring it on!

177
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,000
[Gon] He's fighting back.

178
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:28,000
[whimpering]

179
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:38,000
[cries out]

180
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:46,000
[grunting]

181
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,000
[sighs]

182
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:15,000
[panting]

183
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:27,000
[Gon continues panting]

184
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:34,000
I did it. I took Hisoka's badge from him.

185
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:36,000
[groans]

186
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,000
[grunts]

187
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:57,000
[footsteps approaching]

188
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:02,000
[man] About 7,000.

189
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:06,000
Do you know what that number represents?

190
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:11,000
That is the number of chances I had
to kill you.

191
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:17,000
But it's also

192
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:21,000
about the number of times you cast
your fishing rod while you were training.

193
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:29,000
Every cast left you wide open,

194
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:33,000
but your focus and your accuracy
were admirable, I'll give you that.

195
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:37,000
And just now, your swing was
equally impressive.

196
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:41,000
But you didn't pay enough attention
to your surroundings.

197
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:45,000
In the future,
remember to watch your back.

198
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:47,000
So long.

199
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:57,000
[Gon] Damn it.

200
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:28,000
[strained breathing]

201
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:40,000
[rustling]

202
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:45,000
[Gon gasps]

203
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:49,000
You surprise me.

204
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:54,000
You hid your presence from me while you
were waiting for your chance to strike.

205
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:59,000
Biding your time until the very moment
that I attacked someone else?

206
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:03,000
Did you learn how to conceal yourself
all on your own?

207
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:04,000
Marvelous.

208
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,000
You're like a wild animal.

209
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:10,000
And your timing was just impeccable.

210
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:13,000
You were able to conceal
your bloodlust

211
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:17,000
by cleverly hiding it behind mine
so that I wouldn't notice.

212
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:19,000
Masterfully done.

213
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:25,000
His blow dart delivered a fast-acting,
powerful muscle relaxant.

214
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:29,000
In a normal person
the effect lasts about ten days.

215
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:31,000
There are three days left.

216
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:34,000
I'm sure by then
you'll make a full recovery.

217
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:37,000
[Gon straining] Wait.

218
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:46,000
If you're not taking your badge
then why are you here?

219
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:49,000
To say, "Congratulations."

220
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:52,000
As it turns out, he was my target.

221
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:56,000
Which means I don't need mine anymore.

222
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:58,000
Well, neither do I.

223
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,000
[Hisoka] Don't be like that.

224
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:02,000
You owe me one now.

225
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:05,000
You can pay me back
whenever you like.

226
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:06,000
So long.

227
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:12,000
[Gon straining]

228
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:18,000
I don't owe you or anybody.

229
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:20,000
Here, take it back.

230
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:24,000
[laughs]

231
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:26,000
I refuse.

232
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:30,000
I've decided to let you live, for now.

233
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:34,000
And I plan to let you continue living
for as long as it suits me.

234
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:39,000
Until some day,
you become truly worthy of killing.

235
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:48,000
I will take it back,

236
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:52,000
but only when you can punch me
in the face like that.

237
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:57,000
In the meantime,
you just hold onto it for me.

238
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:03,000
[Hisoka laughs]

239
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:45,000
[narrator]
Gon was knocked out by Hisoka's punch

240
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:47,000
and realized he was utterly helpless

241
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:49,000
in the face of such power.

242
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:52,000
And now, alone in the darkness,

243
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:55,000
what must be going through his mind?

244
00:21:57,000 --> 00:21:59,000
[theme song playing]

245
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:21,000
[Gon] Next time:
"Trap x in x the Hole."

246
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:22,000
Holy moly.

247
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:26,000
-I want to be your friend.
-Wow. Friend?

248
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:28,000
You're embarrassing.
